  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a baseline for the multimodal approach (the study's primary hypothesis) using standard, well-understood components to reduce uncertainty about overall feasibility. config_001 uses multimodal + multiprofile with pca_n2000 (cheap, standard RNA representation), resnet50 (standard image encoder), avgpool (simple aggregation), and weighted fusion (common fusion strategy). This tests whether a straightforward multimodal pipeline achieves competitive validation accuracy and provides a reference point for all subsequent ablations (e.g., swapping encoders, aggregation, or fusion). It is a moderate-cost experiment—cheaper than configurations using imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, or scgpt—so it preserves GPU budget for more expensive explorations in later experiments. Starting here lets me quickly determine whether multimodal fusion is beneficial and which component (RNA encoder, image encoder, aggregation, fusion) is most likely to be the bottleneck, guiding the remaining 9 experiments efficiently."
